{"availability":"available","full":"guilhermefeitosa66/OpenEmux","name":"OpenEmux","description":"Linux-native emulator frontend (GTK4/Python) inspired by OpenEmu","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":27,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-14T21:05:18Z","updated":"2026-10-09T00:46:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"develop","homepage":"https://guilhermefeitosa66.github.io/OpenEmux/","topics":[],"demo":"https://guilhermefeitosa66.github.io/OpenEmux/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:19.193Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:19.193Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:19.193Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:24.912Z","stars":26,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:56:19.193Z","stars":27,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A beautiful, Linux-native emulation frontend that makes RetroArch simple and enjoyable for everyone.","RetroArch is one of the most powerful and versatile emulation platforms ever created — but its interface can be intimidating, especially for users who just want to pick up a controller and play. OpenEmux wraps RetroArch in a clean, intuitive frontend so you can enjoy your retro game library without touching a single config file.","OpenEmux was directly inspired by OpenEmu, the beloved macOS emulator that made retro gaming on Mac feel effortless and beautiful. Since OpenEmu is exclusive to macOS, I built OpenEmux to bring that same polished experience to Linux."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilhermefeitosa66/OpenEmux/blob/develop/README.md","fingerprint":"79f46045fb9ca6605167d5a38a132895eac491634f8e0fb2b6d3f418f34cdd03","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:25.058Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:25.058Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A beautiful, Linux-native emulation frontend that makes RetroArch simple and enjoyable for everyone.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guilhermefeitosa66/OpenEmux/blob/develop/R